/*! 
\page GEOMEC_3D Geomec 3D

This page introduces the Geomec 3D model (C3DModel). Geomec 3D supports a \ref GEOMEC_HEXA or \ref GEOMEC_TETRA . A \ref GEOMEC_2D model is generated by intersecting a Geomec 3D model.

Geomec 3D models are constructed from surfaces (CSurfaceBase). Surfaces are imported by Gocad files (CGoCadFile), ASCII files (CElementSetFile) or Excel files (CElementSetExcel). The Gocad files and element set files (ASCII or EXcel files with the SURFACE file format import connected surfaces. It is also possible to import a surface by point set (CPointSet). Three columns are given: the Easting, Northing and Surface column. The column with the Surface tag are the depth values of the surface and is the surface meshed by the CSurfaceValueType. The mesh is generated by the CTSSurface of the TS library. This library is quite unstable and it is better to replace it by the Triangle library to get rid of the TS library. The surfaces are attached to deratives of the C3DHorizon. The meshing (CMeshBase::CreateMesh) results in C3DFormation object owner of CFormationVolume containing the generated elements. geo::CInterfaceElement are generated for slipping horizons.
After meshing and assigning IMaterial to C3DFormation and assigning CPressure values to each CDepletionStage an analysis is made by running CGeomec3DDianaRunner.

\section GEOMEC_SHORT Well paths

The well path (CWellPath) reprents a well trajectory through the formations (CFormationBase) of the model. The CWellPath is derived from the well::CWellPathBase of the WellScheme library. Geomec supports vertical wells and deviated wells (well::CWellPath::IsVertical). A vertical well is straight line at certain Easting Northing location along the Z-Axis defined by two points (CGeoWellPoint). A deviated well is defined definition points (CGeoWellPoint, well::CWellPathBase::DefPointList)  (well::with a certain Along Hole Depth (AHD) (well::CWellPoint::TMD), an azimuth angle (well::CWellPoint::Azimuth) and an inclination (well::CWellPoint::Inclination) angle. The well head is positioned by an Easting-Northing (well::CWellPathBase::GlobalEasting, well::CWellPathBase::GlobalNorthing) location and a derick elevation (well::CWellPath::GlobalTVD).
The well path intersects the C3DMesh of the C3DModel with CWellPath::CalculateMeshIntersecPoints. These CGeoWellPoint objects are stored in the CWellPath::MeshIntersecPoints point list (well::CWellPointList). The CGeoWellPoint intersection the formations (C3DFormation) are calculated in CWellPath::CalculateFormationIntersecPoints and stored in CWellPath::FormationIntersecPoints. These points are used for defining the CFormationSection in CWellPath::UpdateFormationSections. 
Results on the wells are visualized in the C2DWellpathGraphScene.
The user can run a DStabor application on a CWellPath by selecting CDStaborWellPoint objects. DStabor is called from the COptimumMudDlg. The DStabor results are accessed by CStaborResult. 
